We need to read input: n, lim, then n integers (50 or 100). Count A and B.

Initialize dp[A][B][0] = 1.

Compute combinations c[i][j] for i up to 50.

Then for k from 1 to 4*n:
   s = k % 2 (1 for forward, 0 for backward? In C, s = k%2; if(s) { forward } else { backward }).
   For i from A down to 0, j from B down to 0:
        dp[i][j][k] = 0;
        if forward (s==1):
            for ii from i to A:
                f = lim - (ii - i)*50;
                if f >= 0:
                    f /= 100;
                    f += j; f = min(f, B);
                    for jj from j to f:
                        if (i != ii || j != jj):
                            dp[i][j][k] += dp[ii][jj][k-1] * c[ii][ii-i] * c[jj][jj-j] mod mod.
        else (backward):
            for ii from 0 to i:
                f = lim - (i - ii)*50;
                if f >= 0:
                    f /= 100; f = max(j - f, 0);
                    for jj from f to j:
                        if (i != ii || j != jj):
                            dp[i][j][k] += dp[ii][jj][k-1] * c[A-ii][i-ii] * c[B-jj][j-jj] mod mod.
        After computing dp[i][j][k], if dp[0][0][k] != 0, print k and dp[0][0][k] and exit.

If loop ends, print "-1\n0".

